diff --git a/Simulator-Connect.md b/Simulator-Connect.md
index 0beb109..cecaf61 100644
--- a/Simulator-Connect.md
+++ b/Simulator-Connect.md
@@ -54,6 +54,11 @@ Your aircraft appears on the map as a **blue top-down high-wing airplane** with
 
 A **heading line** runs ahead of the icon, marked at 2 / 5 / 10 nm and at 2 / 5 min; in a turn it becomes a quarter circle bending the way you turn, with the distance marks only (see [The heading line](GPS-Track-Recording#the-heading-line)). The footer shows ground speed, altitude and magnetic heading from the sim feed, and the [in-flight alerts](GPS-Track-Recording#in-flight-alerts) — next leg, TOP, altitude, drift, off route — run off a simulator position exactly as they do off a GPS fix, which is the easiest way to try them on the ground.
 
+**⏺ Record** while connected records the **simulator's flight**, not the device GPS. A recording
+that Record started on the device GPS before the simulator connected carries on from the
+simulator, and Location goes off (one you turned on yourself stays on, and the GPS keeps
+precedence). Disconnecting the simulator ends its recording and saves it.
